130
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,000
There's too much.

131
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:01,000
And so instead of doing something, we just get overwhelmed, and oftentimes we do nothing.

132
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Not only that, we get overstimulated, we get distracted, we're so busy, our lives are so busy,

133
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:12,000
that when needs do arise, when it comes obvious to us that there is an opportunity for us to meet a need,

134
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:16,000
we're too busy to be bothered to meet the need right in front of us.

135
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:21,000
We're overstimulated, we're easily distracted.

136
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:28,000
And what can we learn from Christ's example of service that might help us serve more effectively in our day and age?

137
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:34,000
Ephesians 2:10 says that God, that we are created in Christ Jesus for good works,

138
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:37,000
which he prepared in advance for us to do.

139
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:41,000
There are some acts of service that you have been called to do.

140
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
You're not called to do them all.

141
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
You're called to do something.

142
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:51,000
There are acts of service that God has prepared in advance for you to do, both intentionally and interruptibly.

143
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:54,000
