00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:47,000
If you have your Bibles, open up to John chapter four and flip your bulletins to the back.

161
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:51,000
John chapter four, starting in verse four.

162
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Read one verse and then we'll read more verses later.

163
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,000
Sound good?

164
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Never mind.

165
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:08,000
Now he had to go through Samaria.

166
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Can you guys say that with me?

167
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
Now he had to go through Samaria.

168
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:28,000
So John starts this story that's going to become a famous story that many of you know by the conversation of Jesus with the woman at the well in Samaria.

169
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:34,000
John starts out this story by saying that Jesus had to go through Samaria.

170
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,000
There's a real emphasis on this like there's no other option.

171
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:39,000
Right?

172
00:11:39,000 --> 00:11:40,000
And Jesus is God.

173
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,000
He's got plenty of options.

174
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,000
He can do what he wants.

175
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:43,000
He can do what he wants.

176
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,000
He's God.

177
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:47,000
And yet John says that Jesus had to go through Samaria.

178
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:58,000
And this is strange language specifically since we know from some cultural writings among the days, especially from Josephus, that many rabbis, Jewish rabbis would avoid going through Samaria altogether.

179
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:04,000
Like there was actually a thing going around in today where they would intentionally avoid Samaria.

180
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:15,000
And so for John to say that Jesus had to go through Samaria, myself and many scholars believe that he's using this term not for geographical reasons, but for theological reasons.

181
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:21,000
He's not saying Jesus had to go through Samaria because it was the only road to get to where he was going.

182
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,000
There was actually other options.

183
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:29,000
He's saying that Jesus had to go through Samaria for some other reason altogether.

184
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:40,000
And I would make the argument that I think Jesus had to go through Samaria on this particular time and this particular day because Jesus had a spiritual call on his life.

185
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:48,000
He had a spiritual call to take a trip through Samaria at this point in his ministry because it was an intentional part of his calling as the Messiah.

186
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:56,000
There are prophecies throughout the Scripture that dictate some things that Jesus, if he is the Messiah, had to do in order to fulfill the promises of the Messiah.

187
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:02,000
And one of those is to unite the northern and southern kingdom of Israel.

188
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:05,000
We read this in Ezekiel chapter 37.

189
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:09,000
This is a prophecy about what Messiah will do when he comes.

190
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
It says, I will make them one nation in the land.

191
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:17,000
On the mountains of Israel, one king shall be king over all of them.

192
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:22,000
My servant David shall be king over them and they shall all have one shepherd.

193
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
I will make a covenant of peace with them.

194
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:27,000
It shall be an everlasting covenant with them.

195
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:35,000
So one thing I think we don't often realize when we read the New Testament is that oftentimes the New Testament talks about Jews.

196
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Jews, it's talking about people from the southern tribes, the three southern tribes, Benjamin, Judah, and Levi.

197
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:48,000
And most of the northern tribes are kind of intermingled into the cultural day.

198
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:57,000
And many of them fall into this category of Samaritan, where they are this group of half Jews who are from the northern tribe and are kind of mixed with the culture of the day.

199
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:02,000
And yet they are still a part of, they are descendants of the promise of the Messiah.

200
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:04,000
They are descendants of the promise of Abraham.

201
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:12,000
And one of Jesus' calls as Messiah is to unite both northern tribe and southern tribe into one nation again.

202
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:24,000
And I believe that this is like the first fruits of God, of Jesus kind of living into this part of his specific calling that he's going to Samaria to engage this group of people.

203
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:33,000
To do the thing that he's been called to do, to unite them into one people who will serve one king and worship on one mountain.

204
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:40,000
Part of who Jesus is and what he came to do included reuniting the northern and southern tribes of the people of Israel.

205
00:14:40,000 --> 00:14:50,000
And this intentional act of service that he had to do, I see as Christ's first act of obedience in this calling, this specific part of the calling on his life.

206
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:52,000
We can read on starting in verse seven.

207
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
He has to go through Samaria.

208
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:59,000
And because he does this, he ends up having a unique conversation with a woman at the well.

209
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:07,000
In verse seven, it says, when a Samaritan woman came down or came to draw water, Jesus said to her, will you give me a drink?

210
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:10,000
His disciples had gone into town to buy food.

211
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:14,000
The Samaritan woman said to him, you are a Jew and I am a Samaritan woman.

212
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
How can you ask me for a drink?

213
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:19,000
For the Jews did not associate with the Samaritans.

214
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Jesus answered her, if you knew the gift of God and who it was that asks you for a drink, you would have asked him and he would have given you living water.

215
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:42,000
Jesus is beginning to engage her in a relationship and a conversation about what she believes and what it is that this division between the Samaritans and the Jews is all about.

216
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,000
And we don't have time to read the whole conversation.

217
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:51,000
But starting in verse 19, she replies to him, sir, the woman said, I can see that you are a prophet.

218
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:54,000
And now she wants to get into theological conversation.

219
00:15:54,000 --> 00:16:03,000
She says, our ancestors worshiped on this mountain, but you Jews claim that the place where we must worship is in Jerusalem.

220
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Woman, Jesus replied, believe me, a time is coming when you will worship the Father neither on this mountain nor in Jerusalem.

221
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:16,000
You Samaritans, worship what you do not know.

222
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:19,000
We worship what we do know for salvation is from the Jews.

223
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Yet a time is coming and has now come when the true worshipers will worship the Father in spirit and in truth.

224
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:29,000
For they are the kind of worshipers the Father seeks.

225
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:33,000
God is spirit and his worshipers must worship in spirit and in truth.

226
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:38,000
The woman said, I know that Messiah called Christ is coming.

227
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
And when he comes, he will explain everything to us.

228
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,000
She's like, I know we've got this debate going on, northern tribe, southern tribe.

229
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:48,000
I know we have disagreements about theology, but we're all waiting for a Messiah.

230
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:51,000
He's going to come and he's going to set us all straight.

231
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Jesus declared, I, the one speaking to you, am he.

232
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Amen.

233
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Jesus, the Messiah, on his call to unite the northern tribes, the southern tribes, and ultimately all of creation underneath the banner of King Jesus has come.

234
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,000
And he is engaging this woman because he had to go.

235
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
He had to go and serve this woman in this way.

236
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:18,000
And what is the result?

237
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,000
And what is the result?

238
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:25,000
The result of this unique conversation on this unique day because Jesus had to go into Samaria is this.

239
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:31,000
In verse 39, it says, many of the Samaritans from that town believed in him because of this woman's testimony.

240
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:36,000
So when the Samaritans came to him, they urged him to stay with him and he stayed two days.

241
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:41,000
And because of his words, many more became believers.

242
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:45,000
They said to the woman, we no longer believe just because of what you said.

243
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Now we have heard for ourselves.

244
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:54,000
And we know that this man really is the savior of the world.

245
00:17:54,000 --> 00:18:04,000
A number of people from the descendants of the northern tribe come to believe that Jesus is the Messiah because of verse four.

246
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Because Jesus had to go through Samaria because he served with intentionality because he had this calling on his life.

247
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:15,000
He knew what he was called to do and he went and he did it.

248
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:21,000
And I think this sets an example for us of how we should think about serving others.

249
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:25,000
This one act of intentional service, it included a divine appointment.

250
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:33,000
And God used that to turn the conversation into the conversion of many Samaritans, which is the first fruit of the prophecies of Ezekiel 37.

251
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:45,000
And although there are a ton of implications for this passage and for us, my primary implication for this morning is that the thing we saw in verse four, that he had to go to Samaria.

252
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:48,000
When we know geographically, he did not have to go.

253
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,000
He went because of his calling.

254
00:18:49,000 --> 00:18:51,000
He went because the spirit led him there.

255
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:59,000
And I believe that we as individuals have callings on our life that God is inviting us to go into, to step into.

256
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:04,000
That there are places and people and things that we have to go and do.

257
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Good works that God created in advance for us to do.

258
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:15,000
And my fear is that we are avoiding doing anything at all because we are so overwhelmed by the great need of the culture around us.

259
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:19,000
He had to go.

260
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Again, I believe that each of us have unique callings, unique thing in our life that God has invited us to do.

261
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:45,000
But oftentimes we're overstimulated by all the opportunities that we don't do anything because we're not sure what the right thing to do is.

262
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:48,000
And today I want to remind us that God did not call us to do everything.

263
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:52,000
He did not call each of one of us to do the same thing.

264
00:19:52,000 --> 00:20:02,000
But there are some things that we, as if you're a follower of Jesus in this room, you have been created in Christ Jesus to do good works, which he prepared in advance for you to do.

265
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,000
There are things that you have to do.

266
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:07,000
Nobody else will do them if you don't do them.

267
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:15,000
There are callings on your life that you are invited to participate with by God through the Holy Spirit that he will use you to do.

268
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:22,000
And unfortunately, unlike Jesus, we don't have like a list of things written down that we have to do, right?

269
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Jesus had prophecies about the Messiah that he had to accomplish.

270
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:31,000
We can't look in the book and be like, what is the thing that Leon is called to do?

271
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:33,000
It's not in there, right?

272
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:35,000
The Holy Spirit has to awaken this in our lives.

273
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,000
We have to discern this from the Holy Spirit and from community.

274
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:45,000
And it has to align with Scripture, but the Scriptures aren't going to give us the specific thing that each one of us are called for.

275
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:50,000
This is why we are invited into relationship with the Holy Spirit.

276
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:59,000
And so on your bulletin, I have this Venn diagram, and I think this can help us when we think about how we are called to serve intentionally.

277
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:03,000
There's this Venn diagram, three Ps because I'm a good Baptist kid.

278
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:08,000
Person, place, and passion.

279
00:21:08,000 --> 00:21:16,000
And I think when we're trying to discern what it is that God might be calling us to, I think we can think about these three descriptors.

280
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:22,000
And I would encourage you to even take some time this week to prayerfully think through this.

281
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:25,000
First person, who are you?

282
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Like, what skills do you have?

283
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,000
What unique abilities do you have?

284
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:31,000
What spiritual gifts has God given you?

285
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:32,000
Who are you?

286
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,000
What has God gifted you to be?

287
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,000
What makes you unique as a person?

288
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:42,000
And many of us struggle to think this way because we compare ourselves to others and we think others are better than we are.

289
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:49,000
But sit in a chair somewhere with the Holy Spirit and ask the Holy Spirit to reveal to you what is special and unique about you.

290
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
What has God gifted you to do?

291
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,000
What skills?

292
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,000
What abilities?

293
00:21:55,000 --> 00:22:02,000
Who are you before a holy and loving God who's inviting you to serve out of your gifting with Him?

294
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Secondly is place.

295
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:07,000
Where do you live, work, and play?

296
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:11,000
Like, who is around you as the person that God has made you to be?

297
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:14,000
Who are the people that God has put you into relationship with?

298
00:22:14,000 --> 00:22:22,000
And most of the time, this will likely be a group of people that we're already in relationship with.

299
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:27,000
But sometimes God puts a calling on your life for a group of people or a place that is not where you live.

300
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:37,000
You guys have heard stories of missionaries receiving this call to go to a foreign land, a distant land, have a burden for a group of people or a situation, and they feel called by God.

301
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:41,000
They feel like there's no option, like they have to go to this place or this thing.

302
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:45,000
And so I don't want to rule that out as a possibility for some of you.

303
00:22:45,000 --> 00:22:49,000
Maybe the Lord is calling you to a place that you aren't currently at.

304
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:56,000
But for most of us, it will likely be a group of people or a relationship or a connection that we already have.

305
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
Who are we?

306
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
Who has God made us to be?

307
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
And where do we live, work, or play?

308
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
What is the place that we exist in?

309
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
And then lastly, passion.

310
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:07,000
What breaks our heart?

311
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:11,000
What hurts us deep down inside?

312
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:17,000
And what needs in my community awaken my passion?

313
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,000
Right?

314
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:27,000
Like, if we look at this menu, you can walk out the door this week, you can turn on the news, and you can see a plethora of things where people are in need in our community.

315
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:36,000
And all of them likely break your heart in some way, shape, or form as a follower of Jesus, or just as a human being who values other human beings.

316
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:45,000
You're likely heartbroken over all kinds of things, but likely there is a few things or a group of things that really just gets you going, gets you fired up.

317
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:48,000
Anybody know what I'm, can you bring it to mind right now?

318
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:51,000
There are things that fire you up.

319
00:23:51,000 --> 00:23:55,000
Where do these things come into alignment with one another?

320
00:23:55,000 --> 00:24:06,000
Who you are, who God's made you to be, what your gifting, your spiritual gifts are, the place that God's called you to be, and then the things that burden you, that break your heart in the midst of this area.

321
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:15,000
I would say, spend some time with this chart, and spend some time with the Holy Spirit, and invite God to give you some wisdom, to eliminate some sections off of the menu, right?

322
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:20,000
It's like, God, I wanna serve you, I wanna do what you're calling me to do, but this is overwhelming.

323
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:24,000
And like, maybe he narrows it down to just the hash browns, I don't know.

324
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:29,000
But we invite the Holy Spirit to give us wisdom, and many of us already have these things.

325
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:36,000
We have a calling, we have a passion, we know what we're called to do, and I would just say, don't grow weary in doing good.

326
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:43,000
If you know what your thing is, if you're already doing your thing, like, don't keep adding more and more things to your plate.

327
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Just stay laser focused on the thing that God is calling you to, and do not grow weary in doing good.

328
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:53,000
Because even when we step out and serve, oftentimes it'll feel like climbing an uphill battle.

329
00:24:53,000 --> 00:25:02,000
We'll have one small victory where we'll see the hope of Jesus strike in somebody's eyes, and we'll feel like we're really making a difference.

330
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:05,000
And then the next week, feel like we're wasting our time.

331
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:09,000
And this is kingdom work in a broken world.

332
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:12,000
And so spend some time with this diagram.

333
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:13,000
Think about it.

334
00:25:13,000 --> 00:25:14,000
Pray about it.

335
00:25:14,000 --> 00:25:15,000
Make a list.

336
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:18,000
And then in your time of prayer, bring it to your community.

337
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:22,000
This is part of the reason that we function in small groups.

338
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:26,000
So you can come to your group and you can say, I really feel like the Lord laid this on my heart.

339
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:32,000
I'm going to go sing a solo at the wherever.

340
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:34,000
I'm going to go hymn sing.

341
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:37,000
And someone in your group goes, nope.

342
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:40,000
God did not call you to go hymn sing.

343
00:25:40,000 --> 00:25:42,000
I can tell you that for sure.

344
00:25:42,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Right?

345
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,000
So there's this important thing that has to happen.

346
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:49,000
We have to do some listening prayer with the Holy Spirit.

347
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:51,000
It has to align with Scripture, right?

348
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:54,000
If we're burdened or passionate about something that Scripture isn't burdened or passionate for,

349
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:56,000
then we're in the wrong spot.

350
00:25:56,000 --> 00:26:01,000
So listening prayer by the Holy Spirit in alignment with the Scriptures,

351
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:06,000
and then encouragement, affirmation from the body of Christ.

352
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:09,000
And sometimes, too, these callings will be seasonal.

353
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:12,000
They can change from period of time to period of time.

354
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:15,000
And sometimes we get locked into an area of ministry.

355
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:17,000
And we think we're supposed to do that ministry for the rest of our life.

356
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:21,000
And we just don't even entertain the idea that God might be calling us to something else

357
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,000
in a different season of our life.

358
00:26:22,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Oftentimes, like parents of young children, you don't have as much time, right?

359
00:26:31,000 --> 00:26:36,000
And so you've got to limit your scope of service so that you can have the biggest impact with the time that you have.

360
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:41,000
And then maybe later in your life, you find yourself with a lot more margin, a lot more bandwidth,

361
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:44,000
and you can then reconsider, God, what is it that you might be wanting me to do?

362
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Should I add another opportunity?

363
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Are you pivoting me to a different calling?

364
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:53,000
And I just think that there are things that God has called you to serve with intentionality in.

365
00:26:53,000 --> 00:26:56,000
And if you're not praying and asking the Holy Spirit to give you wisdom,

366
00:26:56,000 --> 00:27:00,000
you'll just be staring at this menu and not doing anything at all.

367
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Does it make sense?

368
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:11,000
I love this quote from Frederick Buechner, would be my guess.

369
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:13,000
I probably should have had Google pronounce it for me.

370
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:20,000
He says, "The place that God calls you to is the place where your deep gladness and the world's deep hunger meet."

371
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:28,000
This is this idea that there is a calling that God has placed on your life and that he's invited you to serve intentionally in a certain area or a certain place.

372
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:35,000
And oftentimes the place is where you as a person get most excited about serving the thing that your community most needs.

373
00:27:36,000 --> 00:27:47,000
And one other thing that I would mention just because one of my things, one of my unique callings is unifying the church.

374
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:54,000
Like unifying denominations and people with different secondary beliefs and political ideologies.

375
00:27:54,000 --> 00:27:56,000
Like I am burdened for the church to be unified.

376
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:59,000
It is one of the things that I know down in my soul that the Lord has called me to.

377
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:03,000
I have to care about unity more than some of you have to care about unity.

378
00:28:03,000 --> 00:28:04,000
That's okay.

379
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:05,000
God's made me this way.

380
00:28:05,000 --> 00:28:13,000
And what I will say is sometimes, sometimes we, unity comes into question when your calling and my calling are different.

381
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:22,000
And when I'm so passionate about this thing that God's called me to do, and you're so passionate about this thing that God's called you to do, we look at each other as enemies.

382
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:29,000
When in reality, it's our unique gifting for God to have a kingdom expression throughout all the places in the world that are broken.

383
00:28:29,000 --> 00:28:38,000
And so like, just like if you're passionate about something over here and somebody else's, I have examples in my head, but I'm afraid to share them.

384
00:28:45,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Yeah, okay.

385
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:47,000
We got you.

386
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:48,000
Thank you.

387
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:50,000
Sometimes our callings will feel.

388
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:51,000
No, let's just do it.

389
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Let's do it.

390
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:53,000
I won't get too specific.

391
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:54,000
I'll go middle of the road.

392
00:28:54,000 --> 00:28:55,000
Partly specific.

393
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:56,000
Tim Keller.

394
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:58,000
You guys like Tim Keller?

395
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:59,000
All right, cool.

396
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:06,000
He often talked about how historic Christianity has four really core moral values in the world.

397
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:09,000
Two of them tend to fall on the right side of the political spectrum.

398
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:11,000
Two of them tend to fall on the left side of the political spectrum.

399
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:18,000
All I will say is sometimes we have Christians who are so called to a specific area of justice and morality that aligns with the right wing party.

400
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:28,000
And some Christians who are called to be passionate and focused on justice on things that might be better absorbed in one political party.

401
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:30,000
And the reality is we're both doing kingdom work.

402
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:40,000
And as long as we're not overly identifying with one political party over the other, we're just doing justice for justice sake in the name of Jesus for the kingdom of God, then let's like unify over that.

403
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:41,000
Sound good?

404
00:29:41,000 --> 00:29:42,000
All right.

405
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,000
Whew.

406
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:44,000
Menu.

407
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:48,000
See, pastors get excited when their illustration works on two levels.

408
00:29:48,000 --> 00:29:50,000
I was so pumped.

409
00:29:50,000 --> 00:29:52,000
I had April laminate this menu.

410
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:55,000
I'm like, this illustration works not on one level, but on two.

411
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:56,000
Intentionality, right?

412
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:01,000
Sometimes we get so distracted by the overwhelming nature of this that we just don't do anything.

413
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:05,000
And also, because we're so overwhelmed, we're so distracted, we're so busy.

414
00:30:05,000 --> 00:30:09,000
And when God offers us an opportunity to serve somebody right in front of us, we can't.

415
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:13,000
Mercer wants to have a conversation with me while I'm looking at the Waffle House menu.

416
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:15,000
Fat chance, all right?

417
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Because I got to figure out what I'm ordering.

418
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:20,000
We can talk after the menu's out of my hand, but before that, nothing.

419
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:29,000
So, secondly, what I want to talk about is how can we, as a people of God, cultivate the value of being interruptible?

420
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:31,000
How can we serve with interruptibility?

421
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:37,000
And I'd love to turn now to Matthew chapter 20 to see another example of Jesus.

422
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:47,000
In John 4, we see Jesus being intentional in his service, that he knows what he's called to do and he's going to go do it, even if it's outside of the realm of cultural acceptance.

423
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:50,000
His disciples are like, why are we going through Samaria?

424
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:51,000
He's like, we have to.

425
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:53,000
We're called to this.

426
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Secondly, Jesus models for us vulnerability.

427
00:30:58,000 --> 00:30:59,000
No, interruptibility.

428
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:03,000
I mean, vulnerability also, but that's not the point for today.

429
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:07,000
Okay, Matthew chapter 20, starting in verse 29.

430
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:12,000
As Jesus and his disciples were leaving Jericho, a large crowd followed him.

431
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Two blind men were sitting by the roadside, and when they had heard that Jesus was going by, they shouted, "Lord, son of David, have mercy on us."

432
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:29,000
The crowd rebuked them and told them to be quiet, but they shouted all the louder, "Lord, son of David, have mercy on us."

433
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:33,000
Jesus stopped and called them.

434
00:31:33,000 --> 00:31:35,000
"What do you want me to do for you?"

435
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:36,000
He asked.

436
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:39,000
"Lord," they answered, "we want our sight."

437
00:31:39,000 --> 00:31:42,000
Jesus had compassion on them.

438
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:49,000
And he touched their eyes and immediately they received their sight and followed him.

439
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:58,000
So for some context, this is at like the climax of Jesus' public ministry, just before he's about to march into Jerusalem on the back of a donkey,

440
00:31:58,000 --> 00:32:02,000
hearing the entire nation of Israel saying, "Hosanna, Messiah, save now.

441
00:32:02,000 --> 00:32:04,000
Jesus, son of David, have compassion on us."

442
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:05,000
It's funny.

443
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:10,000
I just now, I just really realized that the blind people are saying the thing that the crowd's going to say in just a little bit.

444
00:32:10,000 --> 00:32:14,000
They know who Jesus is, they're begging him for mercy.

445
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:22,000
And it's at the climax of his popularity in his earthly ministry, just before his triumphal entry, when he's got places to be and people to see.

446
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:34,000
When he's far busier and on far more of a significant journey than any of us will ever be on, that he is able to be interrupted by two people that the rest of the crowd says ignore them.

447
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:35,000
They're not worth your time.

448
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:36,000
They're not worth your time.

449
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:37,000
You've got too many important things to do.

450
00:32:37,000 --> 00:32:40,000
Jesus, you have places to be and people to see.

451
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:49,000
And yet Jesus is able to, at the height of the speed of his ministry, just moving quickly and the crowds following him and ushering him towards Jerusalem.

452
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:51,000
He's able to be interruptible.

453
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:55,000
He's able to have compassion on these individuals.

454
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:59,000
This word compassion is splachizomai.

455
00:32:59,000 --> 00:33:00,000
You say that?

456
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:01,000
Splachizomai.

457
00:33:01,000 --> 00:33:06,000
It is a word that typically is only used of Jesus having compassion.

458
00:33:06,000 --> 00:33:16,000
It's the one we read about in the parable of the Good Samaritan a few months back, that the Good Samaritan representing Jesus in that parable had compassion on this individual who was left for dead.

459
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:25,000
And Jesus is able to have compassion, a compassion that can keep him from being so preoccupied with the busyness of his day.

460
00:33:25,000 --> 00:33:32,000
So preoccupied with his task list that he can't be bothered to help somebody in need.

461
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:34,000
Jesus flips the script.

462
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:39,000
He shows us that to be truly human is to see image bearers of deserving of dignity and compassion.

463
00:33:39,000 --> 00:33:45,000
His heart breaks for them and he dignifies them by having a conversation with them.

464
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:50,000
And not only that, but he heals them in miraculous ways.

465
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:59,000
And I would say that from this passage, we see that just like Jesus sets an example for us to serve with intentionality, he also sets an example for us to serve with interruptibility.

466
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:02,000
And we have to cultivate this attitude.

467
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:05,000
We're not just gonna be easily interruptible.

468
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:15,000
I think many Christians, sorry, I skipped ahead of my notes.

469
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:20,000
I think as Christians, we have unique people or groups of people we are intentionally called to serve.

470
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:32,000
But I also think that these good works prepared in advance that we talked about in Ephesians chapter two, that there are also good works in advance that are just seemingly random acts of kindness done when we are prompted by the Holy Spirit.

471
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:36,000
But in order for us to be prompted by the Holy Spirit, we have to be listening to the Holy Spirit.

472
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:40,000
In order for us to listen to the Holy Spirit, we have to have some space and some margin in our life.

473
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:42,000
We have to take the AirPods out of our ears.

474
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:44,000
And that is a message directly to me.

475
00:34:44,000 --> 00:34:45,000
My wife knows it.

476
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:46,000
I'm not even gonna look over there.

477
00:34:46,000 --> 00:34:47,000
We got to take the AirPods out.

478
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:50,000
We don't need to be listening to a podcast 24/7.

479
00:34:50,000 --> 00:34:53,000
We got to put the phone down and we have to be interruptible.

480
00:34:53,000 --> 00:34:56,000
We have to be able to see people and dignify them.

481
00:34:56,000 --> 00:35:03,000
In order for us to hear the Spirit and respond to his invitation, we have to be paying attention.

482
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:09,000
And I think many Christians have been lulled into kingdom uselessness through overactivity.

483
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:12,000
We try and do all the things the world says we should do.

484
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:13,000
We're in all the sporting events.

485
00:35:13,000 --> 00:35:14,000
We're in all the clubs.

486
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:15,000
We're in all the activities.

487
00:35:15,000 --> 00:35:20,000
We do all the things the world tells us to do and all the things the church tells us to do.

488
00:35:20,000 --> 00:35:23,000
And we're busier than any other human being on our cul-de-sac.

489
00:35:23,000 --> 00:35:29,000
And we don't take time to stop and ask what it is that God actually wants us to do.

490
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:38,000
We just get caught up in the tide of the world around us.

491
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:45,000
We're doing everything with our children and with our families and with our communities that the world tells us we're supposed to.

492
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:47,000
And what the church tells us we're supposed to.

493
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:52,000
And we're inactive to serve the way that God might be calling us to serve.

494
00:35:55,000 --> 00:36:00,000
I was on a Zoom call.

495
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:03,000
You guys, we agreed on the tithing extra 10 minutes?

496
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:04,000
Six minutes.

497
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:05,000
Six.

498
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Okay, perfect, perfect, perfect.

499
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:07,000
Oh, yeah.

500
00:36:07,000 --> 00:36:08,000
That's better math, Gary.

501
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:09,000
Thank you.

502
00:36:09,000 --> 00:36:10,000
Six.

503
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:11,000
I got six minutes.

504
00:36:11,000 --> 00:36:12,000
Extra six minutes.

505
00:36:12,000 --> 00:36:21,000
I got on a call recently with a seminary professor and he was talking about this idea of missional living, intentionally living on mission and being interruptible and being able to serve others.

506
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:30,000
And he was talking to his students and he was like, I wonder what, if you could ask your neighbors what it is they think most defines Christians.

507
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:32,000
Like, what are the things that they would say?

508
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:35,000
And he was just having this hypothetical conversation with them.

509
00:36:35,000 --> 00:36:41,000
But one of his students decided that she was going to go to all of her neighbors and tell her it was an assignment, which I love.

510
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:43,000
I love her intentionality behind that.

511
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:48,000
She's like, I want to know what my neighbors think mostly define Christian values.

512
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:52,000
And so she had lived on the same cul-de-sac with like a bunch of neighbors.

513
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:53,000
They'd all been there for 10 to 15 years.

514
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:55,000
And she went around to each one of them.

515
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:56,000
She was like, hey, you know, I'm a Christian.

516
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:59,000
What is it that you think makes Christianity?

517
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:03,000
Like, what are our values as a Christian family?

518
00:37:03,000 --> 00:37:07,000
And she said the overwhelming majority of people said, well, you're really busy.

519
00:37:07,000 --> 00:37:12,000
You, like, leave your house way more often than the rest of us do.

520
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:23,000
And I just think, I think that if we're not careful, we're trying to keep up with the Joneses in our culture and we're also trying to do everything the church needs us to do.

521
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:31,000
And we're just moving at such a fast pace that we don't stop to think, God, is this something that you would be inviting me to do?

522
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:39,000
Or is this something that I'm just doing because I think it makes me a good parent or a good spouse or a good friend or a good neighbor or coworker or whatever?

523
00:37:39,000 --> 00:37:41,000
What is it that God is calling us to do?

524
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:46,000
In order for us to do this, we've got to be slowing down a little bit.

525
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:48,000
I love Dallas Willard's quote.

526
00:37:48,000 --> 00:37:50,000
You guys, many of you have probably heard this.

527
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:57,000
Someone asked him, what do I need to, what is the most important thing for me to do to become the person that God is calling me to be?

528
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:03,000
Dallas Willard took a deep breath and he said, you must ruthlessly eliminate hurry from your life.

529
00:38:03,000 --> 00:38:09,000
Talked about if the devil can't get you to sin, he'll just keep you busy.

530
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:16,000
That oftentimes we miss out on opportunities to serve because we're too busy.

531
00:38:16,000 --> 00:38:18,000
Our life just moves too quickly.

532
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:24,000
I just want to remind us this morning that the idea of being conformed to the image of Jesus isn't just about sinning less,

533
00:38:24,000 --> 00:38:27,000
but it's about obeying more.

534
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:30,000
And we cannot obey the invitations that we haven't heard.

535
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:34,000
And how will we hear the invitations if we are not listening?

536
00:38:34,000 --> 00:38:46,000
Just think that maybe, just maybe we're missing out on some obedience to Jesus because we're not listening for his invitation to the prompting of the Holy Spirit.

537
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:53,000
And again, you're going to walk out the door today and you're going to live your life this next week.

538
00:38:53,000 --> 00:39:00,000
And there will be so many opportunities for you to serve interruptibly that if you took the every opportunity to serve interruptibly,

539
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:03,000
you would not fulfill the duties of your life.

540
00:39:03,000 --> 00:39:06,000
And so I'm not saying you have to do everything.

541
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:13,000
When we did the parables series, there's a scholar by the name of Klein Snodgrass.

542
00:39:13,000 --> 00:39:15,000
We got all kinds of cool names today.

543
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:21,000
And he talked about this idea of the New Testament being an identity book, not a guidebook.

544
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:28,000
So when the New Testament talks to us about being interruptibly or serving with interruptibility,

545
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:32,000
it's not saying that every time you're interrupted with the need, you have to serve.

546
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:37,000
It's saying that Christians are a people who are interruptible and who serve interruptibly.

547
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:39,000
I nailed that, by the way.

548
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:43,000
Thank you.

549
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:44,000
Okay.

550
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:54,000
So I think the same thing, listening to the Holy Spirit, asking God to reveal to us the opportunities he's invited us to step into and serve and do so by the power of his spirit.

551
00:39:54,000 --> 00:40:04,000
Not for credit, not so we can put it on social media, but so that we can dignify other human beings, so we can do the thing that Jesus did for these blind people.

552
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:07,000
He had compassion on them and he miraculously healed them.

553
00:40:07,000 --> 00:40:14,000
We have a message, the gospel, that can do far more than just heal a blind person.

554
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:16,000
It can give them eternal life.

555
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:21,000
Are we having compassion on people and taking the message of Jesus with them?

556
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:23,000
All right, next Venn diagram.

557
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:43,000
So I think when it comes to cultivating interruptibility, I want you to, this week, just take some time with this Venn diagram and think about these three areas of your life, your home, your church, your vocation, whatever that might be.

558
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:48,000
And make a list of things that you invest time in in these three areas.

559
00:40:48,000 --> 00:40:51,000
What takes up most of your time while you're at home?

560
00:40:51,000 --> 00:40:55,000
What are the things that take up most of your time, the things that you're involved in at church?

561
00:40:55,000 --> 00:41:00,000
What are the regular activities and rhythms of just being a part of a church community?

562
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:07,000
And what are the things that are going on at work or your vocation, whatever that might be.

563
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:09,000
And make a list.

564
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:15,000
And as you look at the list, think about, are there anything, are there any of these things on the list that I could take off?

565
00:41:15,000 --> 00:41:22,000
Are there any of these things on the list that I'm just doing because I feel like I'm supposed to, but actually like I really don't need to do it?

566
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:29,000
Are there any things on the list that you need to do, but you could do less of?

567
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:34,000
And notice, I'm just going to, I'm going to pat myself on the back really quickly.

568
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:40,000
You are hearing from a pastor on stage at a church that maybe you might be called to do less things at church.

569
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:44,000
Have you heard that before?

570
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:47,000
It's really hard for me to say.

571
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:50,000
I got to be honest with you because I'd love for you to do more stuff here.

572
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:58,000
But maybe, just maybe you're doing too much in this building and you're not interruptible outside of this building with the kingdom of God.

573
00:41:58,000 --> 00:42:00,000
Like most of us in here already have the kingdom of God.

574
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:11,000
So if we're so busy, so preoccupied with a group of people that already have the kingdom of God that we can't be interruptible outside, then maybe we're doing too much inside.

575
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:14,000
What can you do less of?

576
00:42:14,000 --> 00:42:20,000
And if you make this list and you're like a hyper proactive type A person and you're like, nah, I'm actually well balanced and I'm interruptible.

577
00:42:20,000 --> 00:42:31,000
Do me a favor and turn on your screen time settings and give someone else that trust access to your screen time.

578
00:42:31,000 --> 00:42:36,000
And then we'll figure that that's the amount of time that you have that you could be interruptible if you want it to be.

579
00:42:36,000 --> 00:42:37,000
Sound good?

580
00:42:37,000 --> 00:42:39,000
That was, anyway.

581
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:44,000
All right, to recap.

582
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Christ sets an example for us.

583
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:51,000
And this is like the foundation of all of it.

584
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:59,000
If we got lost in the practicality of how to serve with intentionality and how to serve with interruptibility, I want to come back and land the plane with this.

585
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:03,000
That Jesus went before us and did this for us.

586
00:43:03,000 --> 00:43:05,000
This is the gospel of Jesus.

587
00:43:05,000 --> 00:43:10,000
The incarnation of Christ shows us that Jesus was interruptible for us at just the right time.

588
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:18,000
He stepped down from heaven to do the will of the Father, to go to the cross, to die on behalf of us for our sins, to raise from the dead.

589
00:43:18,000 --> 00:43:23,000
Promising us new life and a future kingdom that is eternal.

590
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:30,000
The actions of Christ show us that he was interruptible and that he was intentional.

591
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:36,000
The Son of Man came not to be served, but to serve and to give his life a ransom for many.

592
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:40,000
This is the foundation of all of it.

593
00:43:40,000 --> 00:43:47,000
Us serving intentionally and with interruptibility is just the practical ramifications of what Jesus has already done for us.

594
00:43:47,000 --> 00:43:54,000
And so first and foremost, I want us to make sure that we understand who it is Jesus is and what it is that he's done for us.

595
00:43:54,000 --> 00:43:57,000
Because he isn't asking you to do anything he hasn't done for you already.

596
00:43:57,000 --> 00:44:02,000
And he isn't asking you to do anything that he won't be with you in as you do it.

597
00:44:02,000 --> 00:44:07,000
And he isn't asking you to do anything that he won't empower you to do by his Holy Spirit.

598
00:44:07,000 --> 00:44:14,000
And he isn't even asking you to care about the results because the results are in his hands, not yours.

599
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:19,000
He's just asking you to step out with intentionality, to follow his example.

600
00:44:19,000 --> 00:44:23,000
His example is what it means to be a real human.

601
00:44:23,000 --> 00:44:31,000
If we want life and flourishing, we follow the example of Jesus because he is the one true human.

602
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:34,000
Perfect, spotless, sinless.

603
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:42,000
The gospel isn't just about blessing the blessings we receive, but it's also about the invitations that we receive.

604
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:45,000
And Jesus has invited us to follow his example to serve.

605
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:50,000
So let's take some time this week with your notes and your bulletin.

606
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:53,000
Pray through these Venn diagrams.

607
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:57,000
Think about what it is that God might be asking you to do or not do.

608
00:44:57,000 --> 00:45:02,000
And the reality is it won't, it will likely not be something massive.

609
00:45:02,000 --> 00:45:12,000
It will likely just be a daily invitation to listen and participate with the Holy Spirit.

610
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:15,000
I love this quote from Mother Teresa.

611
00:45:15,000 --> 00:45:17,000
It sums this whole thing up.

612
00:45:17,000 --> 00:45:19,000
She says, God loves us.

613
00:45:19,000 --> 00:45:20,000
That's the gospel.

614
00:45:20,000 --> 00:45:22,000
God loves you.

615
00:45:22,000 --> 00:45:25,000
He doesn't love you for what you can do for him.

616
00:45:25,000 --> 00:45:28,000
He just loves you.

617
00:45:28,000 --> 00:45:33,000
And because he loves you, we have the opportunity to love others as he loves us.

618
00:45:33,000 --> 00:45:37,000
Not in big things, but in small things done with great love.

619
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:44,000
As the band come up, I think the song we ended with is a good reminder.

620
00:45:44,000 --> 00:45:50,000
That Christ has set for us an example.

621
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:54,000
That he's gone before us and that he invites us to follow.

622
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:59,000
I love this line, my one life endeavor to match your surrender.

623
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:01,000
To mirror not my will, but yours.

624
00:46:01,000 --> 00:46:07,000
May this not be just a song that we sing, but it may be a lifestyle.

625
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:13,000
That we look to the example of Jesus who was interrupted on our behalf.

626
00:46:13,000 --> 00:46:18,000
Who was intentional to come, to die, to raise, and to ascend.

627
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:23,000
May everything we do flow out of a desire to follow his surrender.

628
00:46:23,000 --> 00:46:26,000
Let's respond to Christ's example this morning in worship.

629
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:27,000
Amen.

630
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:28,000
Amen.

631
00:46:28,000 --> 00:46:29,000
Amen.
